5,1,1,talk,Misaki,,The feature lists are noise. I care about who actually runs this after the switch.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Kenji,,The yard equipment is ancient. I need to know if the new system can talk to those old devices without breaking.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Toshio,,Headline prices hide the real cost. I need to see what keeps arriving after the initial approval.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Yumi,,I worry about who is actually in charge when things break. I want to see if the plan stays true to the business.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,I am concerned about systems that quietly age in place. I need to see the upgrade history to understand how we handle obsolescence.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, if the devices fail, the crews on the floor are the ones stuck. I need to know their capacity.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, exactly. The crews are the real bottleneck. I am checking the yard devices and the 2021 scheduling trial to see if they can handle the load.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, obsolescence is a cost trap. I will check the five years of renewal invoices to see the true recurring burden.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, recurring costs are scary, but I am more worried about the human side. Who actually fixes things when they break?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
