35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The data is stark. Two key admins retire this year, and the last hire took eleven months. We are critically understaffed.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, that staffing gap is terrifying. My yard data shows the 2021 trial failed because spreadsheets took over. We need a system that survives our chaotic peak season.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, the trial failure is a warning. My invoices show add-ons climbing yearly, while bundled deals held steady. I will check the board minutes to see how these costs are approved.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, that cost creep is worrying. But my outage data is worse: support sat unowned for two days! Who is actually in charge when things break?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, unowned support is a symptom of the deeper rot. My dispatch history shows three skipped upgrades; we are just patching a decaying core.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, unowned support confirms the human gap. With admins leaving, we cannot rely on external fixes. We need a vendor who trains our remaining staff deeply.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Yumi, unowned support is a disaster. My yard data shows the 2021 trial failed because spreadsheets took over. We need a system that survives our chaotic peak season.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, unowned support is a symptom. My board minutes show capital requests trimmed for three years, while operating lines pass easily. We are locked into recurring costs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Misaki, you are right. The two-day gap proves we need a single, accountable owner. I will check the warehouse rule changes to see if the plan survives contact with reality.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, that recurring trap is exactly what I fear. My 2018 data lift took a year to fix. We need a vendor who owns the migration, not just the software.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, the supervisors dropped the standard steps. If the new system is complex, they will ignore it too. We need simplicity.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
